  ('cbrs_units__CoastalBarrierResourcesSystem-3', 'CBRS Units', 'Floodplains', 'floodplain_wetland', 'https://cbrsgis.wim.usgs.gov/arcgis/rest/services/CoastalBarrierResourcesSystem/MapServer', 3, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 30, 'high', NULL),
  ('coastal_zone_management_act__CoastalZoneManagementAct-0', 'Coastal Zone Management Act', 'Floodplains', 'floodplain_wetland', 'https://coast.noaa.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Hosted/CoastalZoneManagementAct/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 30, 'high', 'These data represent the extent of the nation''s coastal zone, as defined by the individual states and territories under the Coastal Zone Management Act of 1972 (CZMA). The CZMA was established to preserve, protect, develop, and where possible, to restore or enhance the resources of the nation''s coastal zone. The zone generally extends seaward to the boundary of the Submerged Lands Act. The zone extends inland from the shorelines only to the extent necessary to control shorelands that have a direct and significant impact on coastal waters. Lands held in trust by the Federal Government have been included in this boundary unless otherwise noted, as accurately representing these could be erroneous. State jurisdiction extends to 3nm, except for Texas, Puerto Rico and Florida’s Gulf coast extends to 9nm. Great Lakes states have jurisdiction to the international boundary with Canada. CZMA applies in EEZ through federal consistency. This boundary is unofficial. For precise regulatory boundaries, please contact the state or territorial coastal program office.'),
  ('noaa_coral_reef_habitat_combined__Coral_Reef_Habitat_Combined-0', 'NOAA - Coral Reef Habitat Combined', 'Floodplains', 'floodplain_wetland', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Coral_Reef_Habitat_Combined/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 30, 'high', 'This dataset combined all of the coral reef habitat layers for FL, HI and the territories. This layer is included in the NTIA Permitting and Environmental Information Application. '),
  ('national_levee_database_leveed_areas__National_Levee_Database___Leveed_Areas-0', 'National Levee Database - Leveed Areas', 'Floodplains', 'floodplain_wetland', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/National_Levee_Database___Leveed_Areas/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 30, 'high', NULL),
  ('national_register_of_historic_places_points__nrhp_points_v1-0', 'National Register of Historic Places - Points', 'Historic Places', 'historic', 'https://services2.arcgis.com/FiaPA4ga0iQKduv3/arcgis/rest/services/nrhp_points_v1/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'point', 15, 'medium', NULL),
  ('national_register_of_historic_places_polygons__NationalRegisterofHistoricPlaces_Polygon-0', 'National Register of Historic Places - Polygons', 'Historic Places', 'historic', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/NationalRegisterofHistoricPlaces_Polygon/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 15, 'medium', 'The National Register of Historic Places is the official Federal list of districts, sites, buildings, structures and objects significant in American history, architecture, archaeology, engineering and culture. The National Historic Preservation Act of 1966 authorized the National Register of Historic Places, expanding Federal recognition to historic properties of local and State significance. The National Park Service in the US Department of the Interior administers both programs. The National Historic Preservation Act authorizes State and Tribal Historic Preservation Officers (SHPOs/THPOs) in each Tribe, State and Territory of the United States to nominate properties to the National Register of Historic Places and to carry out other preservation activities. Federal Preservation Officers (FPOs) have been designated in Federal agencies to nominate Federal properties and to fulfill other responsibilities under the Act. Properties listed in the National Register of Historic Places possess historic significance and integrity and take the form of either a building, site, structure, object or district. Properties listed on or eligible for the National Register of Historic Places must receive consideration based on the National Historic Preservation Act prior to any undertaking involving Federal monies. Additionally, properties listed on or eligible for the National Register may receive grants, tax credits and other benefits based on their status under the National Historic Preservation Act.

This data was downloaded on 02/14/2025 from here: https://irma.nps.gov/DataStore/Reference/Profile/2210280'),
  ('alabama_state_lands__StateLands-0', 'Alabama State Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://conservationgis.alabama.gov/adcnrweb/rest/services/StateLands/MapServer', 0, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('university_of_alaska_lands__Investment_and_Educational_Properties_All_Regions_Public_View-11', 'University of Alaska Lands', 'Alaska', 'state_protected', 'https://services.arcgis.com/2j08Y1PuezhQEfCz/arcgis/rest/services/Investment_and_Educational_Properties_All_Regions_Public_View/FeatureServer', 11, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('legislative_designated_area__SurfaceClassification_LegislativelyDesignatedAreas-0', 'Legislative Designated Area', 'Alaska', 'state_protected', 'https://arcgis.dnr.alaska.gov/arcgis/rest/services/OpenData/SurfaceClassification_LegislativelyDesignatedAreas/MapServer', 0, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('state_parks__Recreational_ParkBoundary-2', 'State Parks', 'Alaska', 'state_protected', 'https://arcgis.dnr.alaska.gov/arcgis/rest/services/OpenData/Recreational_ParkBoundary/MapServer', 2, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('state_forests__State_Forest_Boundary_Public_View_2-0', 'State Forests', 'Alaska', 'state_protected', 'https://services1.arcgis.com/7HDiw78fcUiM2BWn/arcgis/rest/services/State_Forest_Boundary_Public_View_2/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('mental_health_trust_land__Ownership_MentalHealthTrustParcels-0', 'Mental Health Trust Land', 'Alaska', 'state_protected', 'https://arcgis.dnr.alaska.gov/arcgis/rest/services/OpenData/Ownership_MentalHealthTrustParcels/MapServer', 0, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('dnr_state_lands__Ownership_StateLandAll-1', 'DNR State Lands', 'Alaska', 'state_protected', 'https://arcgis.dnr.alaska.gov/arcgis/rest/services/OpenData/Ownership_StateLandAll/MapServer', 1, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('arizona_state_trust_parcels__State_Trust_Parcels-0', 'Arizona - State Trust Parcels', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://server.azgeo.az.gov/arcgis/rest/services/azland/State_Trust_Parcels/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This data set represents surface state trust parcels in Arizona. A surface state trust parcel in Arizona is a piece of state trust land where the State holds and manages the surface rights (for uses such as grazing, agriculture, commercial leases), while the mineral or subsurface rights may be held or leased separately. '),
  ('arkansas_public_lands__Planning_Cadastre-16', 'Arkansas - Public Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://gis.arkansas.gov/arcgis/rest/services/FEATURESERVICES/Planning_Cadastre/FeatureServer', 16, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('california_land_ownership__ownership-0', 'California - Land Ownership', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://egis.fire.ca.gov/arcgis/rest/services/FRAP/ownership/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', '<p style=''margin: 0in 0in 4.5pt; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;''><font size=''3'' style=''font-family: inherit;''>This dataset is intended to provide the best available statewide depiction of land ownership in California. It includes lands owned by federal agencies, state agencies, local government entities, conservation organizations, special districts, etc. It does not include lands that are in private ownership.</font><br /></p><p style=''margin: 0in 0in 4.5pt; font-family: &quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;''><font size=''3'' style=''font-family: inherit;''><br /></font></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>This dataset was updated internally April, 2023 and online June 2023. </p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>This ownership dataset was generated primarily from CPAD data, which already tracks the majority of ownership information in California. CPAD is utilized without any snapping or clipping to FRA/SRA/LRA. CPAD has some important data gaps, so additional data sources are used to supplement the CPAD data. Currently this includes the most currently available data from BIA, DOD, and FWS. Additional sources may be added in subsequent versions. Decision rules were developed to identify priority layers in areas of overlap.</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>Starting in 2022, the ownership dataset was compiled using a new methodology. Previous versions attempted to match federal ownership boundaries to the FRA footprint, and used a manual process for checking and tracking Federal ownership changes within the FRA, with CPAD ownership information only being used for SRA and LRA lands. The manual portion of that process was proving difficult to maintain, and the new method (described below) was developed in order to decrease the manual workload, and increase accountability by using an automated process by which any final ownership designation could be traced back to a specific dataset.</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''><span style=''font-family: inherit; font-weight: bold;''>The current process for compiling the data sources includes:</span></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* Clipping input datasets to the California boundary</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* Filtering the FWS data on the Primary Interest field to exclude lands that are managed by but not owned by FWS (ex: Leases, Easements, etc)</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* Supplementing the BIA Pacific Region Surface Trust lands data with the Western Region portion of the LAR dataset which extends into California.</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* Filtering the BIA data to exclude areas that represent only mineral rights rather than surface ownership.</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* In the case of overlap, sources were prioritized as follows: FWS &gt; BIA &gt; CPAD &gt; DOD</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* As an exception to the above, DOD lands on FRA which overlapped with CPAD lands that were incorrectly coded as non-Federal were treated as an override, such that the DOD designation could win out over CPAD.</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>In addition to this ownership dataset, a supplemental _source dataset is available which designates the source that was used to determine the ownership in this dataset.</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''><span style=''font-family: inherit; font-weight: bold;''>Data Sources:</span></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* GreenInfo Network''s California Protected Areas Database (CPAD2022b). <a href=''https://www.calands.org/cpad/'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>https://www.calands.org/cpad/</a>; <a href=''https://www.calands.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/CPAD-2022b-Database-Manual.pdf'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>https://www.calands.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/CPAD-2022b-Database-Manual.pdf</a></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* US Fish and Wildlife Service FWSInterest dataset (updated February, 2023). <a href=''https://fws.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=0a30eaf43328427db8750282d67f0005'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>https://fws.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=0a30eaf43328427db8750282d67f0005</a>or <a href=''https://ecos.fws.gov/ServCat/Reference/Profile/144384'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>https://ecos.fws.gov/ServCat/Reference/Profile/144384</a>or <a href=''https://services.arcgis.com/QVENGdaPbd4LUkLV/arcgis/rest/services/FWSInterest/FeatureServer'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>https://services.arcgis.com/QVENGdaPbd4LUkLV/arcgis/rest/services/FWSInterest/FeatureServer</a></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* Department of Defense MIRTA dataset (updated 2022) <a href=''https://www.acq.osd.mil/eie/BSI/BEI_DISDI.html'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>https://www.acq.osd.mil/eie/BSI/BEI_DISDI.html</a></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* Bureau of Indian Affairs, Pacific Region, Surface Trust and Pacific Region Office (PRO) land boundaries data (2023) via John Mosley <a href=''mailto:John.Mosley@bia.gov'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>John.Mosley@bia.gov</a></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''>* Bureau of Indian Affairs, Land Area Representations (LAR) and BIA Regions datasets (updated Oct 2019) <a href=''https://biamaps.doi.gov/bogs/datadownload.html'' style=''color: rgb(90, 147, 89); text-decoration-line: none; font-family: inherit;''>https://biamaps.doi.gov/bogs/datadownload.html</a></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''><span style=''font-family: inherit; font-weight: bold;''>Data Gaps &amp; Changes:</span></p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''><span style=''font-family: inherit; font-weight: bold;''>23_1: </span>A few discrepancies were discovered between data changes that occurred in CPAD when compared with parcel data. These issues will be taken to CPAD for clarification for future updates, but for ownership23_1 it reflects the data as it was coded in CPAD at the time. In addition, there was a change in the DOD input data between last year and this year, with the removal of Camp Pendleton. An inquiry was sent for clarification on this change, but for ownership23_1 it reflects the data per the DOD input dataset.</p><p style=''margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 6px; padding-bottom: 1em; font-family: &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13.3333px;''><span style=''font-family: inherit; font-weight: bold;''>22_1 : </span>represents an initial version of ownership with a new methodology which was developed under a short timeframe. A comparison with previous versions of ownership highlighted the some data gaps with the current version. Some of these known gaps include several BOR, ACE and Navy lands which were not included in CPAD nor the DOD MIRTA dataset. Our hope for future versions is to refine the process by pulling in additional data sources to fill in some of those data gaps. In addition, any topological errors (like overlaps or gaps) that exist in the input datasets may thus carry over to the ownership dataset. Ideally, any feedback received about missing or inaccurate data can be taken back to the relevant source data where appropriate, so fixes can occur in the source data, instead of just in this dataset.</p>'),
  ('colorado_parks_and_wildfire_managed_properties__CPWAdminData-5', 'Colorado - Parks and Wildfire Managed Properties', 'Colorado', 'state_protected', 'https://services5.arcgis.com/ttNGmDvKQA7oeDQ3/arcgis/rest/services/CPWAdminData/FeatureServer', 5, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'CPW Administrative Boundary AGOL hosted web service data to provide public access to CPW data including CPW Facilities, Roads, Trails, Gold Medal Waters, Property Ownership, Game Management Units, Walk In Access Program, and Organizational Boundaries'),
  ('colorado_state_land_board_lands__Colorado_State_Land_Board_Lands-0', 'Colorado State Land Board Lands', 'Colorado', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Colorado_State_Land_Board_Lands/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This layer is from the State of Colorado and shows the lands owned by the state land board. The state lands are used to generate funding for Colorado public schools. This layer is added to the NBAM for permitting NEPA review. '),
  ('connecticut_dept_of_energy_and_environmental_protection_prop__Connecticut_DEEP_Property-0', 'Connecticut -Dept. of Energy and Environmental Protection Property', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services1.arcgis.com/FjPcSmEFuDYlIdKC/arcgis/rest/services/Connecticut_DEEP_Property/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'DEEP Property contains property that comprises DEEP facilities such as state forests, parks, and wildlife management areas.'),
  ('delaware_protected_natural_resources_nature_preserves__DE_Protected_Natural_Resources-8', 'Delaware Protected Natural Resources - Nature Preserves', 'Delaware', 'state_protected', 'https://enterprise.firstmap.delaware.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Environmental/DE_Protected_Natural_Resources/MapServer', 8, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'No Build Lines and Points - To ensure that beaches and dunes are able to perform their protective and recreational functions, construction must be kept off them. A Building Line has been established along the coast as part of the Regulations Governing Beach Protection and the Use of Beaches. The Building Line, which parallels the coastline, is designated on DNREC maps. No construction may take place seaward of the Line without a Coastal Construction Permit or Coastal Construction Letter of Approval from the Department of Natural Resources and Environmental Control(DNREC).Park Facilities - outdoor recreational facilities throughout Delaware.Natural Areas - boundaries for the Natural Areas Inventory statewide for the purpose of achieving voluntary land protection of the most important natural areas in Delaware.Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program Lands – Lands where Delaware Land &amp; Water Conservation Trust Fund (now the Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program) monies have been invested.Land and Water Conservation Fund – Lands protected under the Land and Water Conservation Fund.Nature Preserves - lands preserved under the Delaware Nature Preserves Program.Outdoor Recreation Areas - The Outdoor Recreation Inventory (ORI) was originally created to track publicly owned lands within Delaware that are open for public recreation. The database has since been expanded to include all publicly and privately owned protected lands (Federal, State, County, Municipal and private conservation) regardless of whether they are open to the public or not.Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program Open Space - land protected in perpetuity under the Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails ProgramPublic Protected Lands – Lands that are publicly owned and open to public access.Conservation Easements - Includes all Conservation Easements held by Delaware State Parks, both current and historic. Also includes a partial &amp; non-comprehensive list of Conservation Easements held by other State agencies and NGOs.Trails and Pathways - Recreational trails and pathwaysSeasonal Restricted Areas - Seasonal Restricted Areas represent portions of Delaware State Parks that are closed to public access during different seasonsPermanent Restricted Areas - Permanent Restricted Areas represent portions of Delaware State Parks that are closed to public access all year long.Wildlife Area Boundaries - Boundaries show the Wildlife Area locations within the State of Delaware.  Some of the boundaries are divided into tracts.'),
  ('delaware_protected_natural_resources_natural_areas__DE_Protected_Natural_Resources-5', 'Delaware Protected Natural Resources - Natural Areas', 'Delaware', 'state_protected', 'https://enterprise.firstmap.delaware.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Environmental/DE_Protected_Natural_Resources/MapServer', 5, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'No Build Lines and Points - To ensure that beaches and dunes are able to perform their protective and recreational functions, construction must be kept off them. A Building Line has been established along the coast as part of the Regulations Governing Beach Protection and the Use of Beaches. The Building Line, which parallels the coastline, is designated on DNREC maps. No construction may take place seaward of the Line without a Coastal Construction Permit or Coastal Construction Letter of Approval from the Department of Natural Resources and Environmental Control(DNREC).Park Facilities - outdoor recreational facilities throughout Delaware.Natural Areas - boundaries for the Natural Areas Inventory statewide for the purpose of achieving voluntary land protection of the most important natural areas in Delaware.Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program Lands – Lands where Delaware Land &amp; Water Conservation Trust Fund (now the Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program) monies have been invested.Land and Water Conservation Fund – Lands protected under the Land and Water Conservation Fund.Nature Preserves - lands preserved under the Delaware Nature Preserves Program.Outdoor Recreation Areas - The Outdoor Recreation Inventory (ORI) was originally created to track publicly owned lands within Delaware that are open for public recreation. The database has since been expanded to include all publicly and privately owned protected lands (Federal, State, County, Municipal and private conservation) regardless of whether they are open to the public or not.Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program Open Space - land protected in perpetuity under the Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails ProgramPublic Protected Lands – Lands that are publicly owned and open to public access.Conservation Easements - Includes all Conservation Easements held by Delaware State Parks, both current and historic. Also includes a partial &amp; non-comprehensive list of Conservation Easements held by other State agencies and NGOs.Trails and Pathways - Recreational trails and pathwaysSeasonal Restricted Areas - Seasonal Restricted Areas represent portions of Delaware State Parks that are closed to public access during different seasonsPermanent Restricted Areas - Permanent Restricted Areas represent portions of Delaware State Parks that are closed to public access all year long.Wildlife Area Boundaries - Boundaries show the Wildlife Area locations within the State of Delaware.  Some of the boundaries are divided into tracts.'),
  ('delaware_public_protected_lands__DE_Protected_Natural_Resources-11', 'Delaware - Public Protected Lands', 'Delaware', 'state_protected', 'https://enterprise.firstmap.delaware.gov/arcgis/rest/services/Environmental/DE_Protected_Natural_Resources/FeatureServer', 11, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'No Build Lines and Points - To ensure that beaches and dunes are able to perform their protective and recreational functions, construction must be kept off them. A Building Line has been established along the coast as part of the Regulations Governing Beach Protection and the Use of Beaches. The Building Line, which parallels the coastline, is designated on DNREC maps. No construction may take place seaward of the Line without a Coastal Construction Permit or Coastal Construction Letter of Approval from the Department of Natural Resources and Environmental Control(DNREC).Park Facilities - outdoor recreational facilities throughout Delaware.Natural Areas - boundaries for the Natural Areas Inventory statewide for the purpose of achieving voluntary land protection of the most important natural areas in Delaware.Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program Lands – Lands where Delaware Land &amp; Water Conservation Trust Fund (now the Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program) monies have been invested.Land and Water Conservation Fund – Lands protected under the Land and Water Conservation Fund.Nature Preserves - lands preserved under the Delaware Nature Preserves Program.Outdoor Recreation Areas - The Outdoor Recreation Inventory (ORI) was originally created to track publicly owned lands within Delaware that are open for public recreation. The database has since been expanded to include all publicly and privately owned protected lands (Federal, State, County, Municipal and private conservation) regardless of whether they are open to the public or not.Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails Program Open Space - land protected in perpetuity under the Outdoor Recreation, Parks and Trails ProgramPublic Protected Lands – Lands that are publicly owned and open to public access.Conservation Easements - Includes all Conservation Easements held by Delaware State Parks, both current and historic. Also includes a partial &amp; non-comprehensive list of Conservation Easements held by other State agencies and NGOs.Trails and Pathways - Recreational trails and pathwaysSeasonal Restricted Areas - Seasonal Restricted Areas represent portions of Delaware State Parks that are closed to public access during different seasonsPermanent Restricted Areas - Permanent Restricted Areas represent portions of Delaware State Parks that are closed to public access all year long.Wildlife Area Boundaries - Boundaries show the Wildlife Area locations within the State of Delaware.  Some of the boundaries are divided into tracts.'),
  ('district_of_columbia_government_land__District_of_Columbia_Government_Land-0', 'District of Columbia -  Government Land', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/District_of_Columbia_Government_Land/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'DC Land was obtained from the DC open data page. Data has been filtered to only showing properties owned by DC. This layer is included in the NTIA Permitting and Environmental Information Application. '),
  ('florida_state_owned_lands__STATE_OWNED_LANDS-0', 'Florida - State Owned Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://ca.dep.state.fl.us/arcgis/rest/services/OpenData/STATE_OWNED_LANDS/MapServer', 0, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This service contains the following:
FL-SOLARIS/LITS State Owned Lands
FL-SOLARIS/CLEAR Conservation Easements - added 5/18/2018
FL-SOLARIS/CLEAR Conservation Owned Lands - added 5/18/2018'),
  ('georgia_dnr_lands__Georgia_DNR_Lands-1', 'Georgia DNR Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Georgia_DNR_Lands/FeatureServer', 1, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This layer shows the lands owned by Georgia DNR. This data was downloaded from: https://georgiawildlife.com/land'),
  ('hawaii_government_lands__ParcelsZoning-23', 'Hawaii - Government Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://geodata.hawaii.gov/arcgis/rest/services/ParcelsZoning/MapServer', 23, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'ParcelsZoning'),
  ('idaho_state_lands__Idaho_State_Lands-0', 'Idaho State Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Idaho_State_Lands/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'Idaho State Lands for the permitting maps.'),
  ('indiana_state_lands__Indiana_State_Lands-0', 'Indiana State Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Indiana_State_Lands/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'Indiana State Lands'),
  ('iowa_public_lands__Public_Lands-0', 'Iowa - Public Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://programs.iowadnr.gov/geospatial/rest/services/Boundaries/Public_Lands/MapServer', 0, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This web service displays public lands in the state of Iowa.  Not all lands shown are open to the public, and signs on the ground should be respected.'),
  ('kansas_public_wildlife_areas__KDWPT_Wildlife_Areas_view-0', 'Kansas - Public Wildlife Areas', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services1.arcgis.com/q2CglofYX6ACNEeu/arcgis/rest/services/KDWPT_Wildlife_Areas_view/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('state_natural_areas__Ky_KNP_Natural_Areas_WGS84WM-0', 'State Natural Areas', 'Kentucky', 'state_protected', 'https://kygisserver.ky.gov/arcgis/rest/services/WGS84WM_Services/Ky_KNP_Natural_Areas_WGS84WM/MapServer', 0, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', NULL),
  ('state_park_boundaries__Ky_State_Parks_Features_WGS84WM-8', 'State Park Boundaries', 'Kentucky', 'state_protected', 'https://kygisserver.ky.gov/arcgis/rest/services/WGS84WM_Services/Ky_State_Parks_Features_WGS84WM/MapServer', 8, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This map service provides access to trail head, campsite, campgrounds, lodging, public structures, and boundaries for State Parks in the Commonwealth of Kentucky.'),
  ('public_hunting_areas__Ky_Public_Hunting_Areas_WGS84WM-1', 'Public Hunting Areas', 'Kentucky', 'state_protected', 'https://kygisserver.ky.gov/arcgis/rest/services/WGS84WM_Services/Ky_Public_Hunting_Areas_WGS84WM/MapServer', 1, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This map service provides access to both open and restricted public hunting areas in the Commonwealth of Kentucky as maintained by KDFWR.'),
  ('state_nature_preserves__Ky_KNP_State_Nature_Preserves_WGS84WM-0', 'State Nature Preserves', 'Kentucky', 'state_protected', 'https://kygisserver.ky.gov/arcgis/rest/services/WGS84WM_Services/Ky_KNP_State_Nature_Preserves_WGS84WM/MapServer', 0, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'A State Nature Preserve is a legally dedicated area that has been recognized for its natural significance and protected by law for scientific and educational purposes. Dedicated state nature preserves are established solely to protect and preserve rare species, the natural environment, or exceptional natural scenery or environmental education opportunities. State Nature Preserves available in this layer are open to the public for hiking only. Hiking trails are closely regulated to protect the natural integrity of the preserve so that it may be passed on unimpaired to future generations. Certain preserves are only open for scientific research at this time and are not available in this layer.'),
  ('state_forests__Ky_StateForests_WGS84WM-1', 'State Forests', 'Kentucky', 'state_protected', 'https://kygisserver.ky.gov/arcgis/rest/services/WGS84WM_Services/Ky_StateForests_WGS84WM/MapServer', 1, 'MapServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'Polygons representing the boundaries of State Forests for the Commonwealth of Kentucky.'),
  ('louisiana_state_lands__Louisiana_State_Lands-0', 'Louisiana - State Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Louisiana_State_Lands/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This layer shows lands owned by the State of Louisiana. The data was downloaded from here: https://www.doa.la.gov/doa/osl/gis-data/  This layer is meant to be used for permitting and environmental review efforts. '),
  ('maine_wildlife_management_areas__MaineDIFW_WildlifeManagementAreas-0', 'Maine - Wildlife Management Areas', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services1.arcgis.com/RbMX0mRVOFNTdLzd/arcgis/rest/services/MaineDIFW_WildlifeManagementAreas/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'Property boundaries of Maine Department of Inland Fisheries and Wildlife''s Wildlife Management Areas derived from Maine Conserved Lands'),
  ('dnr_owned_lands_and_conservation_easements__MD_ProtectedLands-0', 'DNR Owned Lands and Conservation Easements', 'Maryland', 'state_protected', 'https://geodata.md.gov/imap/rest/services/Environment/MD_ProtectedLands/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'Polygon boundaries of various protected lands in Maryland including: DNR Owned Properties and Conservation Easements, Rural Legacy Properties, MD Environmental Trust Easements, Forest Conservation Act Easements, MD Agricultural Land Preservation Foundation Easements, Local Protected Lands, Coastal and Estuarine Land Conservation Program, Private Conservation Lands and Protected Federal Lands.

Information on the number of acres protected in Maryland can be found on the Maryland Protected Lands Reporting site at http://dnrweb.dnr.state.md.us/gis/plreports/.
'),
  ('local_protected_lands__MD_ProtectedLands-5', 'Local Protected Lands', 'Maryland', 'state_protected', 'https://geodata.md.gov/imap/rest/services/Environment/MD_ProtectedLands/FeatureServer', 5, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'Polygon boundaries of various protected lands in Maryland including: DNR Owned Properties and Conservation Easements, Rural Legacy Properties, MD Environmental Trust Easements, Forest Conservation Act Easements, MD Agricultural Land Preservation Foundation Easements, Local Protected Lands, Coastal and Estuarine Land Conservation Program, Private Conservation Lands and Protected Federal Lands.

Information on the number of acres protected in Maryland can be found on the Maryland Protected Lands Reporting site at http://dnrweb.dnr.state.md.us/gis/plreports/.
'),
  ('massachusetts_public_open_space__MD_OpenSpace_Public-0', 'Massachusetts - Public Open Space', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/MD_OpenSpace_Public/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This layer shows public open spaces in Maryland at the local and state level. This data was downloaded here: https://www.mass.gov/info-details/massgis-data-protected-and-recreational-openspace  The data was filtered to remove Federal and private lands. This layer is meant to be used for permitting and environmental review purposes. '),
  ('minnesota_state_administered_lands__Minnesota_State_Administered_Lands-0', 'Minnesota - State Administered Lands', 'State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Minnesota_State_Administered_Lands/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'This layer depicts state administered lands in Minnesota. The layer was downloaded from here: https://gisdata.mn.gov/dataset/bdry-dnr-managed-areas  Federal areas were removed from the dataset. This layer is meant to be used by permitting and environmental review. '),
  ('state_parks__Mississippi_State_Parks_and_WMAs-0', 'State Parks', 'Mississippi - State Lands', 'state_protected', 'https://services3.arcgis.com/OYP7N6mAJJCyH6hd/arcgis/rest/services/Mississippi_State_Parks_and_WMAs/FeatureServer', 0, 'FeatureServer', 'polygon', 5, 'low', 'Mississippi State Parks and Wildlife Management Areas.')
